A change to the Python maze, for the e2e "changed" check (explore --changed): its hunks are
lines of the new file. The first runs in every timeline, the second where the first digit is
right (one timeline in ten, which the targeted tree returns to), the third only where the maze
is solved (never, in a run this short).
--- a/tests/antithesis-compat/python/client/maze/singleton_driver_maze.py
+++ b/tests/antithesis-compat/python/client/maze/singleton_driver_maze.py
@@ -24 +24 @@
+det.always(not solved, "the maze is never solved")
@@ -17 +17 @@
+    det.reachable("maze: first digit")
@@ -23 +23 @@
+                solved = True
